// What the engine may ask for after Ingest (plan P1-19; design T9 A1) — the
// one vocabulary of the resource pull. Read by tools/gen-res.mjs, which
// generates the column tables of both codecs: engine/src/resource/
// resources.gen.h and runtime/src/shared/resources.gen.mjs (the wire format
// is docs/host-protocol-design.md §5).
//
// Admission rule: a row is a datum the engine can obtain only after Ingest,
// keyed by content the engine computes. Anything known before Ingest is a
// setting or a declared input, never a resource.
//
// RES_VERSION(n): raised by any change of a row or of the wire format.
// RES(name, id, cache, docProviders, "key columns", "answer columns")
//   cache:        Content (answers are a function of the key: a session may
//                 keep them) | Host (only the host's cache, with validators) |
//                 None
//   docProviders: whether a document-registered provider may answer (keys of
//                 authored content only)
//   columns:      name:type, types Str (a string of the batch's blob),
//                 MetricKey (a row of the batch's metric-key table), U8, U16,
//                 U32, F64, U32List
RES_VERSION(3)
RES(textWidth, 1, Content, false, "mk:MetricKey text:Str", "px:F64")
RES(fontVmet, 2, Content, false, "mk:MetricKey", "asc:F64 desc:F64")
RES(fontFace, 3, None, false, "family:Str src:Str weight:U16 style:U8", "status:U8")
RES(codeTokens, 4, Content, true, "lang:Str text:Str", "runs:U32List")
RES(boxInfo, 5, Host, true, "kind:U8 ref:Str availPx:F64", "w:F64 h:F64 baseline:F64")
// (plan P4-06; D-X09) a language's hyphenation patterns, asked for once per
// language tag the document's text names (en-US is resident): TeX pattern
// text, exceptions as hyphenated words, the minima, the hyphen glyph
RES(hyphPatterns, 6, Content, false, "lang:Str", "patterns:Str exceptions:Str leftmin:U8 rightmin:U8 hyphenChar:Str")
// (plan P5-01; D-M03) a face's reference ink: the ink ascent of "H" and the
// ink descent of "p" — per style, like fontVmet (v2 §6) — asked for only
// under math.referenceInk, for a formula's text-font runs
RES(fontInk, 7, Content, false, "mk:MetricKey", "asc:F64 desc:F64")
